body:
Addressed: No finding was fixed. The conflict rule requires a stop because both sides change the same tab-window descent logic.

I merged current `upstream/main` (`3593a61235bc0f5d9ad0ec9dc9e0526c67ed45e7`) into the PR worktree. The merge conflicted in `contour.rs` and `contour_step.rs`.

The blocking hunk is in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour.rs`, in the tab-window branch of `emit_band`:

```rust
<<<<<<< HEAD
                tab_window_dive(b, p, e2, hop_z, lead_top);
=======
                // Tab window to tab window: up over the tab, across, down (pecked, #3678).
                let cur = b.at();
                b.push(MoveKind::Feed, Point3::new(cur.x, cur.y, hop_z), Some(p.feed));
                b.push(MoveKind::Rapid, Point3::new(e2.x, e2.y, hop_z), None);
                super::contour_link::guard(b, p, e2, lead_top, p.entry_top(), "the dive past a tab");
                let (pf, uncut) = (p.plunge_feed, uncut_floor(p, rz, rzi));
                dive(b, p, e2, lead_top, uncut, hop_z, pf, |b, d| b.push(MoveKind::Plunge, Point3::new(e2.x, e2.y, d), Some(pf)));
>>>>>>> upstream/main
```

Other hunks overlap the imports, the `Step` initializer, and the `Step` fields (`traverse` and `uncut`).

I aborted the merge. The warm worktree is clean and remains at `.claude/worktrees/fix-3921`.
The PR head is unchanged: `77b71f78b216efea67651394267e860eff081877`.
No commit or push was made. No tests, mutation checks, quick gate, heavy gate, catalog suites, or clippy ran.
A re-review of a fix is pending resolution of this stop condition.
